  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 155 PM CDT Fri Oct 9 2026\n\nSouthwesterly low level winds, 850 mb temps of 16-17C, and \napproaching upper ridging has allowed temperatures to surge \nback into the 80s today. We may approach record highs in a few \nlocations. The upper level ridging will pass through the area \ntonight, with weak high pressure at the surface allowing for \nlight winds. Hurricane Isaias, which is currently in the Gulf of\nAmerica just off the coast of the AL/FL border, is expected to \nmove north and make a slight jog to the left/west by early \nSaturday morning. The remnants are expected to cross KY on \nSunday, but there continues to be some uncertainty regarding the\ntrack. Based on the current forecast model suite, there's only \na 10-15% chance of 1\" or more of rain in the far southeastern \nzones Saturday night into Sunday. Dry air will be in place today\nand Saturday ahead of the moisture surge. The above normal \ntemperatures and dry fuels will elevate fire danger slightly \nthis afternoon. Thankfully, winds are rather light, staying \naround 15 mph or less. Increased cloud cover and dew points will\nhelp limit fire danger on Saturday.\n\nAs the upper level low (remnants of Isaias) moves east on \nSunday, an upper ridge will build in over the Midwest in it's \nwake. Temperatures will rebound to near record levels in the \nupper 80s to lower 90s on Monday. To the north, an upper wave \nwill ride the ridge through MN/WI Monday night, suppressing the\nridge a bit and pushing a cold front south through IL on \nTuesday. A few showers/storms are possible with this front. A \nbetter chance for rain comes on Tuesday night and Wednesday as \nan upper wave ejects from the Central Plains ahead of a Central \nRockies upper low. The upper low is expected to merge with a \nCanadian low, deepening into a large upper low over the \nNorthern Plains by Thursday. Tuesday night through Thursday \nlooks active (several chances of rain) followed by a push of \ncold air. Some of the latest model runs have temps at 850 mb \nnext Saturday around -6 to -2C. The best you can get for \ndaytime highs with that is maybe 50 degrees. The Grand Ensemble\nof models has a 30% chance of 850 mb temps less than 0C on\nSaturday. We'll see how things evolve.",
